[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.75]
\coordinate (M) at (0,0);
\coordinate (N) at (4.4,0);
\coordinate (T) at (2.985,4.109);
\draw (M)--(N) node[midway,below] {$120\text{ m}$};
\draw (M)--(T);
\draw (N)--(T);
\pic[draw,"$54^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.4] {angle=N--M--T};
\pic[draw,"$71^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=1.45] {angle=T--N--M};
\node[below left] at (M) {$M$};
\node[below right] at (N) {$N$};
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Markers $M$ and $N$ are $120$ m apart. The angle to a tower $T$ is $54^{\circ}$ from $M$ and $71^{\circ}$ from $N$. Find the distance $NT$, correct to $1$ decimal place.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\coordinate (E) at (4.4,0);
\coordinate (F) at (1.826,3.294);
\draw (D)--(E) node[midway,below] {$3.5\text{ km}$};
\draw (D)--(F);
\draw (E)--(F);
\pic[draw,"$61^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=1.4] {angle=E--D--F};
\pic[draw,"$52^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=1.4] {angle=F--E--D};
\node[below left] at (D) {$D$};
\node[below right] at (E) {$E$};
\node[above] at (F) {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Cross-country markers $D$, $E$ and $F$ have $\angle D=61^{\circ}$, $\angle E=52^{\circ}$ and leg $DE=3.5$ km. Find the length of leg $EF$, correct to $2$ decimal places.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (G) at (0,0);
\coordinate (H) at (4.4,0);
\coordinate (K) at (2.915,2.915);
\draw (G)--(H) node[midway,below] {$18\text{ m}$};
\draw (G)--(K);
\draw (H)--(K);
\pic[draw,"$45^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=1.4] {angle=H--G--K};
\pic[draw,"$63^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=1.45] {angle=K--H--G};
\node[below left] at (G) {$G$};
\node[below right] at (H) {$H$};
\node[above] at (K) {$K$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A triangular garden $GHK$ has $\angle G=45^{\circ}$, $\angle H=63^{\circ}$ and side $GH=18$ m. Find the perimeter of the garden, correct to $1$ decimal place.
